.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MIRRORD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mirrord
.Nd mirrortools background daemon service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Op Fl socket Ar path
.Op Fl http Ar addr
.Op Fl password Ar pass
.Op Fl password-file Ar path
.Op Fl concurrency Ar n
.Op Fl db Ar path
.Nm
.Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the background daemon for
.Xr mirror 1 .
It manages a persistent queue of mirror requests, executes them with
configurable worker concurrency, quarantines problematic or failing jobs,
and provides both a local Unix domain socket for CLI management and an
HTTP server for the Web dashboard and REST API.
.Pp
Mirror jobs and execution logs are stored in a SQLite database, ensuring
jobs survive service restarts.
Requests submitted through
.Ic mirror queue submit
are dispatched to worker slots and logged in real time.
.Pp
The flags are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl config Ar path
Configuration file to read.
The default is
.Pa ~/.config/mirrortools/config.toml
or
.Ev $MIRROR_CONFIG .
.It Fl socket Ar path
Path to the Unix domain socket for local control.
The default is
.Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/mirrortools/mirrord.sock
or
.Pa ~/.local/state/mirrortools/mirrord.sock .
.It Fl http Ar addr
TCP address and port for the Web UI and HTTP API, such as
.Li 127.0.0.1:8080 .
When omitted or empty, only the local Unix domain socket is used.
.It Fl password Ar pass
Password protecting the Web UI and HTTP API.
.It Fl password-file Ar path
Path to a file containing the password protecting the Web UI and HTTP API.
.It Fl concurrency Ar n
Maximum number of worker goroutines running mirror jobs simultaneously.
The default is 2.
.It Fl db Ar path
Path to the SQLite database file.
The default is
.Pa ~/.local/state/mirrortools/mirrord.db .
.It Fl version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh QUEUE MANAGEMENT
Jobs in the queue move through several states:
.Bl -tag -width quarantined -compact -offset indent
.It Sy queued
Waiting for an available worker slot.
.It Sy running
Currently being downloaded by a worker.
.It Sy paused
Held from execution until resumed.
.It Sy completed
Successfully finished.
.It Sy failed
Finished with an error, eligible for retry.
.It Sy quarantined
Isolated after repeated failures or authentication/ban errors.
.It Sy cancelled
Explicitly terminated by the user.
.El
.Pp
A job that encounters repeated errors (by default 3) or non-transient
authentication/permission errors (such as HTTP 403 Forbidden or expired
credentials) is automatically quarantined so it does not waste worker
slots or risk remote IP bans.
Quarantined jobs can be reviewed and retried using
.Ic mirror queue unquarantine .
.Sh WEB UI
When started with
.Fl http Ar addr ,
.Nm
serves an embedded, self-contained single-page dashboard.
The Web UI provides real-time job monitoring, queue pause/resume controls,
live log streaming via Server-Sent Events (SSE), manual submission, and
in-browser configuration editing.
.Sh AUTHENTICATION
When an HTTP listener is configured, authentication can be enabled to protect
the Web dashboard and REST API.
Local CLI operations over the Unix domain socket remain unauthenticated,
protected by local filesystem permissions.
.Pp
Two authentication mechanisms are supported:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy Password authentication
Configured with
.Fl password ,
.Fl password-file ,
or in
.Li [daemon.auth]
with
.Li password
or
.Li password-file .
In the browser, logging in sets a secure, HTTP-only session cookie.
For API requests, the password may be sent via
.Li Authorization: Bearer <password>
or HTTP Basic authentication.
.It Sy OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect
Configured under
.Li [daemon.auth.oauth]
with provider settings
.Li provider ,
.Li issuer
or endpoints
.Pq Li auth-url , token-url , userinfo-url ,
.Li client-id ,
and
.Li client-secret
or
.Li client-secret-file .
Optional user authorization can be restricted using
.Li allowed-users .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/mirrortools/config.toml
The configuration file.
Daemon settings go in the
.Li [daemon]
section.
.It Pa ~/.local/state/mirrortools/mirrord.db
The SQLite database storing jobs, history, and log messages.
.It Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/mirrortools/mirrord.sock
The local control socket.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mirror 1 ,
.Xr mirrorq 1
